# TLS terminator + reverse proxy for apps/api (docs/tasks/TASK-aws-infra.md §2.4).
#
# renewable-pulse.duckdns.org is a free DuckDNS name with an A record set by hand to the
# instance's Elastic IP (52.5.78.81). The IP never changes, so there is no dynamic-DNS updater.
# duckdns.org is on the Public Suffix List, so Let's Encrypt rate limits are per-name, not
# shared with every DuckDNS user. Certificates are the standard 90-day ones; Caddy issues and
# renews them automatically over HTTP-01 on port 80.
#
# Tried first and abandoned (2026-09-27): a Let's Encrypt IP-address certificate on the bare EIP
# with `issuer acme { profile shortlived }`. The HTTP-01 challenge validated, but finalize
# returned "403 unauthorized: authorizations for these identifiers not valid" on Caddy 2.11.4,
# even though the adapted config did carry profile=shortlived.

renewable-pulse.duckdns.org {
	encode zstd gzip

	# Also carries the /live WebSocket upgrade; reverse_proxy handles that natively.
	reverse_proxy api:3001
}
